WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.670
All right, let's go to our color from the
five one nine area code.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.650
Who's calling today from five one nine.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.440
Hi David, this is Jesse.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.719
Hey Jesse, what's going on?

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:12.719
Not too much.

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:16.299
I'm a huge fan of your show and I really appreciate
you having your life.

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:17.340
Thank you.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.030
Um, I just have two questions for you.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:27.810
Uh, the one is, do you think the left is giving
their power away by not giving enough empathy

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.710
to people on the right?

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:35.360
Maybe even Donald Trump, you know, kind of
dehumanizing him and being sort of vicious

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.910
and losing sight of, you know, the fact that
he's just a person.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.910
And B,

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:41.910
I don't know.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.910
Well, hold on, let's take it one at a time.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:44.320
How is the left dehumanizing Trump?

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.210
I see a lot more dehumanization coming from
Trump than to Trump.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.320
Oh, absolutely.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:55.940
So what I'm saying, like I'm a progressive
and that's one of the reasons why I've watched

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:01.620
your show because you're very balanced in
your judgments, but you also, um, are kind

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.670
of a lefty electing himself, it seems like.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:09.740
So what I'm saying is even though we have
people who do terrible things, at the end

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:15.110
of the day, when we stop treating them like
people and start treating them like monsters,

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.840
it almost gives them more power in a sense.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:19.249
Would you agree with that?

00:01:19.249 --> 00:01:22.329
I think that there are circumstances in which
that's true.

00:01:22.329 --> 00:01:23.329
Yeah.

00:01:23.329 --> 00:01:24.329
Yeah.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:29.399
And it kind of leads into my second question
is do you think the left, um, and some of

00:01:29.399 --> 00:01:35.380
the, uh, public speakers on the left, like
even nuts or, uh, talk show host some, uh,

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:42.130
what have you, like Stephen Colbert evangelize
Trump's brand more than they, uh, take them

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:46.399
down in a sense?

00:01:46.399 --> 00:01:47.399
You mean inadvertently?

00:01:47.399 --> 00:01:48.399
Yeah.

00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:54.461
So I noticed that, um, ever since Donald Trump
started running for presidency, uh, Steven

00:01:54.461 --> 00:01:59.509
Cole bear can't help but discuss Trump and
this seems like a widespread thing on the

00:01:59.509 --> 00:02:00.509
left.

00:02:00.509 --> 00:02:01.509
Yeah.

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:05.749
And my concern, I live in Canada by the way,
so I'm just kind of watching everything unfold.

00:02:05.749 --> 00:02:13.159
Um, my concern is that by always focusing
on him and making him a monster, not kind

00:02:13.159 --> 00:02:15.610
of bringing it down to a human level.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:19.790
And if they don't stop talking about him,
they're actually evangelizing.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:20.790
I dunno.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:25.170
I mean, listen, you can make the case that
if you just, if media literally pays no attention

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:28.160
to someone, that person becomes no one because
they go away.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:29.930
Trump is the president of the United States.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.900
He would still be doing things even if people
didn't pay attention.

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:36.989
And people wouldn't be aware of the things
that he is doing, which are objectively bad.

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:38.989
So I understand the point you're trying to
make.

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:40.909
I think it's more about finding a balance.

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:44.909
But no, I have no particular reason to think
that someone like Stephen Colbert has actually

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:47.129
evangelizing for Trumpism.

00:02:47.129 --> 00:02:48.129
Okay.

00:02:48.129 --> 00:02:52.140
Um, well thank you so much, uh, for your time
today.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.319
I really appreciate it.

00:02:53.319 --> 00:02:54.870
All right, Jesse, appreciate the phone call.

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:55.480
Thank you so much.

